Project Architecture

This is where they may ask:

“Can you explain the architecture of your IDTR project?”

Your answer should be based on what you actually built—not pretend that it was Clean Architecture.

Your project was essentially:

UI / Screen
     ↓
Provider
     ↓
HTTP API
     ↓
Backend

And data comes back:

Backend
   ↓
HTTP response
   ↓
Provider
   ↓
notifyListeners()
   ↓
UI rebuild

For example:

CourseScreen
     ↓
CourseProvider
     ↓
GET /api/courses
     ↓
API response
     ↓
CourseProvider updates data
     ↓
notifyListeners()
     ↓
Consumer rebuilds UI

This is actually a good interview explanation because it demonstrates that you understand data flow, rather than just saying "I used Provider."

Flutter's current architecture guidance describes this general idea as separation of concerns and unidirectional data flow: user interaction goes toward the data/logic layer, and updated state flows back toward the UI.

Important correction for your interview

Don't say:

"My architecture is Provider architecture."

Better:

"The application uses a screen-based feature structure with Provider for state management. Screens handle presentation, providers handle state and API interaction, and models represent API data."

That's more accurate.